system "ISO:ell-Grek:Latn:843-1997-t1" {

metadata {
  authority_id iso
  id 843-1997-t1
  language iso-639-2:ell
  source_script Grek
  destination_script Latn
  name "ISO 843:1997 Information and documentation -- Conversion of Greek characters into Latin characters (Table 1)"
  url https://www.iso.org/standard/5215.html
  creation_date 1997
  description {    Establishes a system for the transliteration and/or transcription
    of Greek characters into Latin characters. This system applies to
    the characters of the Greek script, independent of the period in
    which it is or was used, i.e. scripts from all periods of Classic
    or Modern Greek. Replaces ISO/R 843.
  }

  notes {
    note "Transliteration of Greek into Latin: Type 1, Clause 3 Table 1"
    note "Equivalent to elot-ell-Grek-Latn-743-2001-tl, the transliteration table of ELOT 743:2001"
    note "Assuming that ou, au, eu transliterations are only intended for historical diphthongs /u, av, ev/, and that όυ, άυ, έυ are not to be transliterated as ou, au, eu"
    note "Introduced casing to digamma, yot, and lunate sigma. (Casing was late introduction to character sets for those characters)"
    note "Table 3, non-alphabetical characters (clause 3.2): tonos/oxia -> acute accent, vareia -> grave accent, perispomeni -> circumflex, dialytika -> diaeresis, psili/koronis -> preceding apostrophe, dasia -> preceding h (dasia over rho yields rh); erotimatiko -> ?, ano teleia -> ;."
    note "Table 3, polytoniko: ypogegrammeni and prosgegrammeni are rendered by a cedilla after the vowel (Table 3 rows 16-17); ano kato teleia -> : passes through."
    note "Table 4, archaic characters (clause 3.2): digamma F -> W/w, giot -> J/j, byzantino (lunate) sigma C -> S/s."
    note "Table 5, Greek numerical symbols (Note 13): a single symbol with the upper numeral sign is converted to its decimal number (alpha'=1 ... theta'=9, koppa'=90, rho'=100 ... omega'=800, sampi'=900, stigma'=6); the lower numeral sign (thousands mark) + letter yields 1000..9000."
    note "Table 5 limitation: multi-symbol numeral groups (e.g. iota-beta' = 12) are not composed by this map; the table defines the correspondence per single symbol only. The myriad block (dot marks = 10000..900000) has no distinct Unicode codepoint (it collides with the teleia full stop) and is not converted."
    note "Note 14: quantity-marked letters (alpha/iota/ypsilon with VRACHY or MACRON, and their capitals) are non-alphabetical marks and are passed through unconverted."
  }
}

tests {
   "Ένα πράμα μόνον με παρακίνησε κι εμένα να γράψω ότι τούτην την πατρίδα την έχομεν όλοι μαζί, και σοφοί κι αμαθείς και πλούσιοι και φτωχοί και πολιτικοί και στρατιωτικοί και οι πλέον μικρότεροι άνθρωποι· όσοι αγωνιστήκαμεν, αναλόγως ο καθείς, έχομεν να ζήσομεν εδώ. Το λοιπόν δουλέψαμεν όλοι μαζί, να την φυλάμεν κι όλοι μαζί και να μην λέγει ούτε ο δυνατός «εγώ» ούτε ο αδύνατος. Ξέρετε πότε να λέγει ο καθείς «εγώ»; Όταν αγωνιστεί μόνος του και φκιάσει ή χαλάσει, να λέγει «εγώ»· όταν όμως αγωνίζονται πολλοί και φκιάνουν, τότε να λένε «εμείς». Είμαστε εις το «εμείς» κι όχι εις το «εγώ». Και εις το εξής να μάθομεν γνώση, αν θέλομεν να φκιάσομεν χωριόν, να ζήσομεν όλοι μαζί.\n\nΓιάννης Μακρυγιάννης.\n" ->  "Éna práma mónon me parakínīse ki eména na grápsō óti toútīn tīn patrída tīn échomen óloi mazí, kai sofoí ki amatheís kai ploúsioi kai ftōchoí kai politikoí kai stratiōtikoí kai oi pléon mikróteroi ánthrōpoi; ósoi agōnistī́kamen, analógōs o katheís, échomen na zī́somen edṓ. To loipón doulépsamen óloi mazí, na tīn fylámen ki óloi mazí kai na mīn légei oúte o dynatós «egṓ» oúte o adýnatos. Xérete póte na légei o katheís «egṓ»? Ótan agōnisteí mónos tou kai fkiásei ī́ chalásei, na légei «egṓ»; ótan ómōs agōnízontai polloí kai fkiánoun, tóte na léne «emeís». Eímaste eis to «emeís» ki óchi eis to «egṓ». Kai eis to exī́s na máthomen gnṓsī, an thélomen na fkiásomen chōrión, na zī́somen óloi mazí.\n\nGiánnīs Makrygiánnīs.\n"
